## 1. Scope

This audit covers audit event persistence, hash chaining, compliance evidence recomputation, exports, reports, evidence packs, runtime/tool audit integration, streaming/export readiness, and UI download behavior. It inspects `product_platform/audit`, `product_platform/compliance`, compliance migrations, artifact repositories, audit/compliance routes in `api/app.py`, and frontend compliance pages. Relevant benchmarks are Microsoft admin/security visibility, LangSmith/Galileo trace/evidence workflows, AWS auditability, JFrog artifact evidence, and enterprise SIEM/export expectations. Out of scope: trace-level observability, covered in OBS.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Audit events are persisted through `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/audit/store.py`, with hash chaining in the same database table. Base audit/event tables are in `0001_base_schema.up.sql`. Compliance controls and evidence use `0044_compliance_controls.up.sql` and `product_platform/compliance/repository.py`. Audit export routes exist around `api/app.py:4521`, and a fixed-list SSE route around `api/app.py:4567`. Tool Gateway runtime action records are in `0055_tool_runtime_actions.up.sql` and `tool_gateway/runtime_audit.py`. The frontend compliance page includes report/download UI in `frontend/src/features/compliance/CompliancePage.tsx`.

Current workflow: the system writes audit events, computes some compliance evidence, can export audit events, and surfaces compliance/report views. The hash chain is useful but not immutable or externally anchored. Compliance recomputation uses fixed limits, evidence packs are summaries, and runtime/tool audit data is not fully unified with compliance exports.

