## 7. Feature-Level Target State

Audit and compliance should form a verifiable evidence graph. Audit events should be append-only, hash-chained, externally anchored, and exportable with proofs. Evidence recomputation should be complete, asynchronous at scale, and tied to source event hashes, policy/control versions, traces, runtime actions, artifacts, and signatures. Tool calls, MCP calls, plugin installs, credential access, and runtime sessions should feed the same evidence model. UI should clearly show export completeness and verification status. Tests should prove tamper detection, pagination, evidence reproducibility, and runtime/tool inclusion.
